  <regions type="content">
    <region left="18" top="9" width="364" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">OptimWrapper - 5x5 linear and nonlinear systems (CAS-defined)</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="45" width="76" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="false">2026-10-24</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="81" width="511" height="263" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">OptimWrapper - two 5x5 systems solved from user-defined CAS residuals</p>
    <p bold="true">GUID 3c9f7e0a-c2b1-4eae-ab68-9ea2c518c510, v1.0.0.0. The plugin has NO built-in</p>
    <p bold="true">test-function ids: the residual systems below are defined here in SMath CAS.</p>
    <p bold="true">Result layout for every solver: column [x1; ...; xn; f; iterations; ok], hence</p>
    <p bold="true">  f = el(res, n+1) = el(res, 6);  ok = el(res, n+3) = el(res, 8)  (n = 5, ok = 1 means converged).</p>
    <p bold="true">LINEAR    (exact x = [2, -1, 3, 1, -2]): optim_broyden on the 5x1 residual matrix.</p>
    <p bold="true">NONLINEAR (exact x = [1, 2, -1, 1, 2]): plain Broyden OVERFLOWS here from a non-root</p>
    <p bold="true">start (ResultIsAboveMaxAllowedPositiveNumber), so the sum of squared residuals is</p>
    <p bold="true">minimised with optim_lbfgs (f ~ 0). Solver variables are x1..x5 (not x, the plot axis).</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="369" width="211" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">2. Initial guesses for the two systems</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
